# Tam, the Possibility: "{W}{U}{B}{R}{G}, {T}: Proliferate X times, where X is the number of planeswalker types among
# planeswalkers you control." Wrenn and Six (type Wrenn) and Oko, Thief of Crowns (type Oko) are two types, so X is two:
# the ability asks twice, and both choices go to Wrenn and Six, whose three loyalty counters become five (CR 701.34a).
# Oko is not chosen, so it stays at four. Tam's own cost reduction paid for Oko's {1}{G}{U} with just {G}{U}. Bot2
# controls Narset, Parter of Veils (type Narset, five loyalty counters): a planeswalker among those "you control" counts
# for its controller only, so X stays two and the refusal after the two answers holds (a third question would be asked
# if Narset counted). The activation costs exactly {W}{U}{B}{R}{G} and taps Tam: six mana is made, so the pool left
# right after is the one spare {G}, and Tam is tapped.

